$CATEGORY: Q14 - Recursive Methods

::Q1401::
leap of faith - 
    A way to read recursive programs by assuming that the recursive call works, rather than following the flow of execution. {TRUE}

::Q1402::
A method or algorithm that repeats steps by using one or more loops.
recursive {
    ~recursive
    =iterative
}

::Q1403::
A method or algorithm that invokes itself one or more times with different arguments.
{
    =recursive
    ~iterative
}

::Q1404::
base case - a condition that causes a recursive method to make another recursive call {FALSE}

::Q1405::
factorial - the product of all the integers up to and including a given integer.
{TRUE}